Third-party

  No third-party code is copied into this product. PyTorch, safetensors, transformers,
  tokenizers and numpy are dependencies, and ttnn an optional one, each installed separately
  under its own license.

  GPTQ follows Frantar et al., "GPTQ: Accurate Post-Training Quantization for Generative
  Pre-trained Transformers" (2022); no code was copied.

  The KL chunking follows llama.cpp's perplexity tool's method (each chunk starting with the
  begin-of-sequence token in place of its first token); no code was copied.

  The calibration and evaluation texts (WikiText-2 and Korean Wikipedia, CC BY-SA) are not
  included; tensix_bfp/data.py downloads them from their sources.
